Concern: re-running one block of a step from a restored residual, after its ops have run
Upstream: not-submitted

The replay of a layer needs two things from radiance that the issue observer (0101) does not give.
First, an op's operands after it ran: the planner reuses transient buffers inside a layer and
across layers, so a snapshot taken at issue time is gone by the time the caller reads it. Second,
an entry point that runs exactly one block of a step: the caller restores the block's input
residual, and the engine clears the block's recurrent state (gdn_chunk_scan reads h0
unconditionally, so a replay that kept the forward's state would start from the wrong h0) and asks
an architecture to issue only that block.

The patch adds a second observer, RadReplayObserver, whose `issued` callback runs after the op has
launched and whose `block` callback sees the same brackets as the issue observer; the two share
the context so a tape and a replay can watch the same step. It adds rad_replay_block /
rad_set_replay_block to the context and Engine::replay_block, which zeros the stateful groups'
slots for the step's sequences (from the batch's own state_index, the same slots the step used) and
runs the step with the block set. The paged KV needs no reset: the batch's used counts and slot map
are the step's start, and the block's own kv_store overwrites every slot it reads.

The qwen35_bf16 step is split so a block's ops, calibration taps included, are one function, the
forward brackets each call, and a replay calls it alone after the embeddings and head are skipped.
clef_bf16 includes the same source, so it gets the same hook.

